(summary: priests' paralysis spells are blocked by MR), though it is useful.

> Other than that, it is a set of characteristics that your character should 
> be or have (and be unable to lose very simply) or have done before 
> attempting the final stage of ascension. Off the top of my head and in 
> general:
> 
> - Level 14 or higher (preferably higher for spellcasters)

This is only needed for the quest. You can ascend being level 1, if you 
manage to get drained after the quest. HP and SP can be gotten from 
potions, though some classes gain useful intrinsics at higher levels. 
You just need enough levels to get all skill slots you want to use, and 
if you cast damage spells, you want as much as possible.

> - At least one method of remote detection of monsters while unblinded; e.g. 
> warning, extrinsic telepathy, astral vision.

Of course what you 'need' to start the final run is highly dependent on 
the player and character, but I think this last one is a pure luxury. As 
you can already deal with everything you might meet, *and* have a viable 
escape in case you can't, you don't need this at all.

